WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.560
All right, next item.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.800
Item seven,
warbird repair and maintenance.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.898
Senator?

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:08.908
Repairs on our ships

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.239
have continually been delayed

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.744
in favor of Klingon
and Federation vessels.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.110
The Dividices

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.274
and the Genorex have been
waiting almost three weeks

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.307
while more than
a dozen Klingon ships

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.512
have been given first priority.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.952
Well, I make up
the repair schedule

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.114
according to my assessment

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.851
of which ships have
the greatest need.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.291
Odd that the Klingons
seem to always have

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.692
the greatest need.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.355
They are usually more damaged

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.627
because Klingon warships
are relentless

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.859
in pressing home their attack.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.993
"Reckless" would be
another way of putting it.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.866
The fight must be taken
to the enemy.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.633
We cannot win this war...

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.503
All right, we're not here
to debate combat tactics.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.975
Chief, how soon can you have
those warbirds

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.238
into a docking bay?

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.143
Well, I suppose I could
bring them in tomorrow.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.374
But that would mean delaying

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:51.009
repairs to the Hornet
and the Rotarran.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.880
Somebody's going
to have to explain

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.547
to General Martok
why his flagship was bumped.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:59.490
Worf, you just volunteered
for that assignment.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.927
This brings up the
question of shore leave.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.123
At the moment, we have the crews

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:07.497
from two Klingon ships
on the station.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:11.231
I'd rather not have that
many Klingons and Romulans

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.239
on the Promenade
at the same time.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.798
We'll forgo shore leave
until the Klingons depart.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.969
Our soldiers are professionals.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.739
They're here to fight

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.179
not to get drunk in Quark's.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.149
All right.
That's it for today then.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.515
Same time next week?

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.519
Oh, sorry, Senator.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.077
You'll be attending
that conference

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.281
on Romulus, won't you?

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.314
Yes, but Subcommander Velal
will be here in my place.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.985
Fine. Have a safe trip.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.322
Thank you.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.223
Ah, yes.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.460
Romulus...

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.991
how well I remember it.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.630
You'll find the predominant
color to be gray...

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.005
the buildings, the
clothes, the people.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.977
Did you know that the Romulan
heart itself is gray?

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.239
It's true.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.305
And altogether appropriate
for such an unimaginative race.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:59.580
I take it you didn't enjoy
your brief stint on Romulus.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.383
You were... posing
as a gardener, weren't you?

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.821
It was one of the few instances

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:06.121
where my cover
was more enjoyable

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.285
than the actual assignment.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.919
What was the assignment anyway?

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.294
I'm afraid
I can't talk about that.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.196
Back to the subject at hand.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.327
What would your role be
at this conference?

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.167
Well, I'll be giving a talk
on Dominion biogenic weapons

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.673
chairing a seminar
on ketracel-white

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.903
and attending a meeting
on a proposal

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:27.504
to transfer 25
Federation hospital ships

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.174
over to Romulan control.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.341
How dull.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.441
Sorry to disappoint.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.678
Admiral Ross and his staff

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.949
will be discussing the
"exciting" military issues.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.717
I see.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.849
I-I trust that
Starfleet Intelligence

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.257
will be sending someone along

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.989
to make good use
of this opportunity.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.188
What do you mean?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.288
Well, isn't it obvious?

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.764
This is a golden opportunity

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.893
to gather intelligence
on Romulan intentions

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.403
and military capabilities.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.098
They're our allies, Garak.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.367
And with any luck

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.568
this could be the beginning
of an entirely new friendship

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.735
between our peoples.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.745
The eternal optimist.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:00.939
Guilty as charged.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.345
How sad.

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:04.179
I must tell you,
I'm disappointed

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.118
at hearing you mouth
the usual platitudes

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.484
of peace and friendship

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:12.958
regarding an implacable foe
like the Romulans.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:17.155
But I live in hope that one day

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:21.099
you'll come to see this universe
for what it truly is

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:23.864
rather than what
you'd wish it to be.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.269
Well, I shall endeavor
to become more cynical

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.967
with each passing day.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.770
Look gift horses
squarely in the mouth

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.371
and find clouds in
every silver lining.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.440
If only you meant it.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.558
Lights.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.364
Sloan.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.959
Hello, Doctor.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.402
It's good to see you.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.804
I hope you're well rested.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.741
Section 31 has
an assignment for you.

00:06:03.695 --> 00:06:04.753
You're taking quite a risk.

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:06.764
I could have a security team
here in 30 seconds.

00:06:06.798 --> 00:06:09.198
I suspect
you'd be unable to communicate

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.758
with anyone
outside of this room.

00:06:10.802 --> 00:06:12.429
I could scream for help.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:13.438
Possible

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:14.734
but uncharacteristic.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.138
I mean, screaming for help...

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.541
that's... that's
too undignified for you.

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:20.442
But don't let me stop you.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:21.946
I enjoy being wrong.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.947
What do you want?

00:06:22.981 --> 00:06:23.743
I told you.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:24.942
You have an assignment.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.677
I don't work for you.

00:06:26.718 --> 00:06:27.776
You passed the test.

00:06:27.819 --> 00:06:29.946
You were accepted
into the organization.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.422
I didn't ask to be accepted.

00:06:32.457 --> 00:06:33.719
You were nevertheless.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.954
And now it's time to go to work.

00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:40.521
I'm sure you're dying to know
what your mission is

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.227
but you won't give me
the satisfaction

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.234
of admitting it.

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:46.294
So I'll just tell you.

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:47.327
Lucky me.

00:06:47.372 --> 00:06:50.967
Section 31
is extremely interested

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:53.068
in this conference of yours.

00:06:53.111 --> 00:06:54.840
However, the Tal Shiar

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.212
will be handling
the security arrangements

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:58.841
so we'll have virtually
no chance

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:02.376
of using any technical assets
to gather intelligence.

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:06.357
As a result, we'll be forced
to rely on organic assets...

00:07:06.391 --> 00:07:07.619
like you.

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:10.890
Your mission is to gather data

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.521
about the Romulan leadership.

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:14.088
In essence, we want you

00:07:14.132 --> 00:07:16.566
to take the pulse
of their government.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.570
No pun intended.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:21.732
You want me to spy on an ally?

00:07:21.773 --> 00:07:24.674
To evaluate an ally.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.304
And a temporary ally at that.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:30.679
Now, I say that, because
when the war is over

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:33.082
the following will happen
in short order...

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:36.576
the Dominion will be forced
back to the Gamma Quadrant.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.785
The Cardassian Empire
will be occupied.

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:43.056
The Klingon Empire will spend
the next ten years recovering

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.893
from the war and won't pose
a serious threat to anyone.

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:50.368
That leaves two powers to vie
for control of the Quadrant...

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:54.270
the Federation and the Romulans.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:55.967
This war isn't over

00:07:56.074 --> 00:07:59.601
and you're already
planning for the next.

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:00.805
Well put.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.906
I hope your report
is equally succinct.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:06.008
How many times do I have
to tell you, Sloan?

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.383
I don't work for you.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.012
You will.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:12.489
It's in your nature.

00:08:12.524 --> 00:08:15.789
You are a man
who loves secrets...

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:19.586
medical, personal, fictional.

00:08:19.631 --> 00:08:23.089
And I am a man of secrets.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:27.936
You want to know what I know
and the only way to do that

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:29.837
is to accept the assignment.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:49.053
Whoa! Easy, Julian.

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:50.823
What's going on?

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.464
Odo's checked
all the security logs.

00:08:57.502 --> 00:08:58.469
There's no indication

00:08:58.503 --> 00:09:00.471
of how Sloan got aboard
or where he went.

00:09:00.505 --> 00:09:01.836
I can't say I'm surprised.

00:09:01.873 --> 00:09:03.397
From what we've seen of them

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:06.411
Section 31 is very meticulous
in covering its tracks.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.744
I had a conversation with
Admiral Ross this afternoon.

00:09:09.781 --> 00:09:12.579
He and I both agree
that the Romulan conference

00:09:12.617 --> 00:09:14.244
is too important to cancel.

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:15.913
What about me?

00:09:16.021 --> 00:09:17.386
Starfleet Command has promised

00:09:17.422 --> 00:09:19.617
to send the expert
on Dominion biogenic weapons

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:22.456
and ketracel-white
to the conference.

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:24.587
Since that's you, you go.

00:09:24.629 --> 00:09:27.029
And we want you to carry out
your assignment.

00:09:27.065 --> 00:09:29.590
Make a few discreet observations
on the Romulan leadership

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:32.660
and then wait for Sloan
to contact you again.

00:09:32.704 --> 00:09:34.171
Somehow, I don't
think giving Sloan

00:09:34.206 --> 00:09:36.140
any information is a good idea.

00:09:36.174 --> 00:09:39.701
That was my instinct as well,
but after talking to Ross

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:42.543
I think we might have
an opportunity here

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.742
we can turn to our advantage.

00:09:44.783 --> 00:09:46.341
Officially, Starfleet Command

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:49.081
has said that they are appalled
at the very notion

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:52.113
that an organization like
Section 31 might exist

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:53.317
and that they plan

00:09:53.358 --> 00:09:56.327
to get to the bottom
of this entire business.

00:09:56.361 --> 00:09:57.885
And unofficially?

00:09:57.929 --> 00:10:01.160
They have quietly
pushed the investigation aside.

00:10:01.199 --> 00:10:04.930
Which means either they
don't take Section 31 seriously

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:08.497
or... someone at Starfleet
Command is protecting them.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:12.874
Either way, we now have a chance
to get someone inside

00:10:12.911 --> 00:10:15.379
and I think I want to take it.

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:16.813
So you want me to play along?

00:10:16.848 --> 00:10:20.340
Pretend that I've decided
to work for Sloan after all?

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:21.613
Exactly.

00:10:21.653 --> 00:10:23.644
When he contacts you to find out

00:10:23.688 --> 00:10:25.121
what you learned
at the conference

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:27.421
make it seem like
you've reluctantly come around

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:28.790
to his way of thinking.

00:10:28.827 --> 00:10:31.387
Let him believe
that he has seduced you

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.397
into helping him.

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:34.228
Well, that shouldn't
be too difficult.

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:35.961
Sloan thinks
I'm already so tempted

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:37.798
that I barely can see straight.

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:40.430
Well, listen, I better pack.

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:42.667
The Bellerophon leaves
in three hours.

00:10:42.707 --> 00:10:45.107
One more thing, Doctor.

00:10:45.143 --> 00:10:47.236
Remember this isn't a game.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.839
Section 31 is very dangerous.

00:10:49.881 --> 00:10:52.611
If Sloan even suspects
that you are really

00:10:52.651 --> 00:10:53.675
working for us...

00:10:53.718 --> 00:10:54.707
I understand.

00:10:59.224 --> 00:11:00.316
Good hunting.

00:11:13.171 --> 00:11:15.105
A glass of Romulan ale,
Doctor?

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.164
Thank you, Senator.

00:11:16.208 --> 00:11:17.675
The trading embargo
has been officially lifted

00:11:17.709 --> 00:11:18.676
if you were wondering.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:20.610
It hadn't crossed
my mind, actually.

00:11:20.645 --> 00:11:23.546
To one of the many benefits
of the alliance.

00:11:28.286 --> 00:11:29.651
Need a medical team, sir?

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:30.985
No, thank you.

00:11:31.022 --> 00:11:33.616
Don't tell me this is
your first glass of Romulan ale.

00:11:33.658 --> 00:11:34.989
Well, it was...

00:11:36.027 --> 00:11:37.756
ille... illegal.

00:11:37.796 --> 00:11:39.229
That never stopped
most of your colleagues.

00:11:39.264 --> 00:11:41.323
I know... I was probably

00:11:41.366 --> 00:11:42.663
one of the few officers
in the fleet

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:44.498
who didn't indulge occasionally.

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:46.868
Would you like something else?

00:11:46.905 --> 00:11:47.929
No, no, I'll manage.

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.634
That's the spirit, sir.
Never say die.

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:52.699
What an odd expression.

00:11:52.744 --> 00:11:53.904
What does it mean?

00:11:53.945 --> 00:11:56.573
It's a line
from an old Earth poem.

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:59.243
Forgive me for interrupting.

00:11:59.284 --> 00:12:00.512
I couldn't help overhearing

00:12:00.552 --> 00:12:03.077
and etymology is
one of my hobbies.

00:12:03.121 --> 00:12:07.251
The, uh, phrase "never
say die" is originally

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:10.193
from a 19th century poem

00:12:10.228 --> 00:12:11.855
based on Shakespeare's
Merchant of Venice.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:15.458
Now, it's since passed
into the vernacular

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.264
as a, as an exhortation
never to give up

00:12:18.303 --> 00:12:19.861
no matter the cost.

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:21.167
Interesting.

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:23.401
Wendell Greer,
Assistant Director

00:12:23.441 --> 00:12:25.966
UFP Department of Cartography.

00:12:26.077 --> 00:12:27.135
It's a pleasure.

00:12:27.178 --> 00:12:29.112
Admiral William Ross,
Senator Cretak.

00:12:29.147 --> 00:12:31.081
Admiral... Senator.

00:12:31.116 --> 00:12:32.447
And Dr. Julian Bashir.

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:36.147
Ah, the physician
from Deep Space 9.

00:12:36.187 --> 00:12:37.677
I was hoping to meet you.

00:12:37.722 --> 00:12:40.987
I have so many questions
about the Bajoran sector...

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:44.655
navigational anomalies,
the transport patterns...

00:12:44.696 --> 00:12:46.163
Could you spare a moment?

00:12:46.197 --> 00:12:47.858
Unless I'm interrupting.

00:12:47.899 --> 00:12:49.093
Not at all.

00:12:53.271 --> 00:12:54.363
Try to play your cards

00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:56.306
a little closer
to your vest, Doctor.

00:12:56.341 --> 00:12:59.504
You're lucky they didn't see
that look of shock on your face.

00:12:59.544 --> 00:13:02.138
You managed to get yourself
attached to this delegation.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.408
Why do you need me?

00:13:03.448 --> 00:13:04.779
All in due time.

00:13:04.816 --> 00:13:07.842
Now you have a lot of work to do
before we arrive at Romulus.

00:13:07.886 --> 00:13:10.377
There's a padd
in your quarters... read it.

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:12.322
I'll join you at 2200.

00:13:16.261 --> 00:13:18.729
Well, Mr. Greer certainly
has his ducks in a row.

00:13:18.763 --> 00:13:20.958
According to the Department
of Cartography

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:23.762
he's been a low-level bureaucrat
for almost 15 years.

00:13:23.802 --> 00:13:26.327
Well, it doesn't surprise me
he has a solid cover story, sir.

00:13:26.371 --> 00:13:28.703
But I think it's too dangerous
to allow him to participate

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.867
in the conference
or even set foot on Romulus.

00:13:30.909 --> 00:13:32.103
We don't know what he's up to.

00:13:32.143 --> 00:13:34.168
On the other hand,
if we move against him now

00:13:34.212 --> 00:13:37.204
we lose any hope
of penetrating Section 31.

00:13:37.248 --> 00:13:40.081
His access at this conference
will be limited

00:13:40.118 --> 00:13:42.086
to a few low-level
briefings and seminars.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.985
It shouldn't be too hard
keeping tabs on him.

00:13:44.055 --> 00:13:46.546
If Sloan's here...

00:13:46.591 --> 00:13:48.821
it suggests something
more important

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.260
than a simple intelligence-
gathering mission.

00:13:51.296 --> 00:13:53.389
He's up to something

00:13:53.431 --> 00:13:56.195
and it's imperative that we
know what that something is.

00:13:56.234 --> 00:13:58.794
We go forward.

00:14:00.071 --> 00:14:01.402
Next.

00:14:01.439 --> 00:14:04.931
Neral... formerly Proconsul

00:14:04.976 --> 00:14:08.468
now Praetor
of the Romulan Star Empire.

00:14:08.513 --> 00:14:10.174
Neral's ascension
to the top post

00:14:10.215 --> 00:14:11.910
was confirmed
by the Continuing Committee

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.178
a little over a year ago.

00:14:13.218 --> 00:14:15.686
His immediate family
was killed in a Klingon raid

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.415
approximately 25 years ago.

00:14:17.455 --> 00:14:20.117
His interests include
sociology and archaeology.

00:14:20.158 --> 00:14:21.785
His favorite food
is Delvan pudding

00:14:21.826 --> 00:14:26.126
and his pet set'leth's name
is... Pensho.

00:14:26.164 --> 00:14:27.222
Very good.

00:14:27.265 --> 00:14:30.598
Total recall is a useful
attribute for an operative.

00:14:34.039 --> 00:14:36.633
Koval... chairman
of the Tal Shiar.

00:14:36.675 --> 00:14:39.269
Section 31 believes that he
was involved in the death

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.971
of Vice Admiral Fujisaki
last year

00:14:41.079 --> 00:14:42.171
but there's no proof.

00:14:42.213 --> 00:14:43.305
The proof is buried

00:14:43.348 --> 00:14:45.578
somewhere in Koval's
personal database

00:14:45.617 --> 00:14:47.414
which puts it
out of our reach for now.

00:14:47.452 --> 00:14:49.647
But believe me, Doctor,
the Deputy Chief

00:14:49.688 --> 00:14:50.916
of Starfleet Intelligence

00:14:50.955 --> 00:14:53.219
doesn't just die
of food poisoning.

00:14:53.258 --> 00:14:55.351
I have to give him credit,
though.

00:14:55.393 --> 00:14:57.088
It was a textbook operation.

00:14:57.128 --> 00:14:58.993
No sign of foul play

00:14:59.097 --> 00:15:02.032
and certainly no sign
of Romulan involvement.

00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:03.762
It was very tidy.

00:15:03.802 --> 00:15:05.929
Koval's political status?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.335
Ambiguous.

00:15:07.372 --> 00:15:09.567
He hasn't been elevated
to the Continuing Committee

00:15:09.607 --> 00:15:12.132
which is usually a given
for the head of the Tal Shiar.

00:15:12.177 --> 00:15:13.667
His nomination has
probably been held up

00:15:13.712 --> 00:15:16.180
because of his opposition
to the Federation alliance

00:15:16.214 --> 00:15:17.306
which is supported

00:15:17.348 --> 00:15:18.815
by the majority
on the Committee.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:22.183
Which, in turn, opens the door
for your friend, Senator Cretak.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.348
She's an advocate
of the alliance

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.790
and she's been lobbying
for this open seat.

00:15:27.826 --> 00:15:30.090
There is another rumor
about Koval

00:15:30.128 --> 00:15:32.961
which is not contained
in his file.

00:15:32.997 --> 00:15:37.434
We've heard he's ill...
something called Tuvan Syndrome.

00:15:37.469 --> 00:15:38.731
I'm familiar with it.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:39.862
It's a neurological disease

00:15:39.904 --> 00:15:42.839
which affects mainly Vulcans,
Romulans and Rigelians.

00:15:42.874 --> 00:15:44.967
It's degenerative,
and incurable at present.

00:15:45.009 --> 00:15:47.773
If Koval is ill,
he'll try to hide it.

00:15:47.812 --> 00:15:50.576
It's a weakness, and
one that could hamper

00:15:50.615 --> 00:15:52.913
his chances of being
appointed to the Committee.

00:15:52.951 --> 00:15:56.512
Is that what I'm here for?
A diagnosis?

00:15:56.554 --> 00:15:57.885
What's the matter, Sloan?

00:15:57.922 --> 00:15:59.981
Doesn't Section 31
have its own doctors?

00:16:00.091 --> 00:16:02.889
Our physicians weren't
genetically enhanced.

00:16:02.927 --> 00:16:04.918
They need equipment
to make a diagnosis...

00:16:04.963 --> 00:16:08.126
equipment that the Romulans
won't permit at this conference.

00:16:08.166 --> 00:16:10.134
I'm incapable
of making a diagnosis

00:16:10.168 --> 00:16:11.726
by simply looking at a man.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:14.295
Oh, your genetically-
enhanced friends

00:16:14.339 --> 00:16:17.206
determined that Gul Damar
killed a woman

00:16:17.242 --> 00:16:19.938
just by watching him
give a political speech.

00:16:20.011 --> 00:16:22.946
I'm sure you can do
better than that.

00:16:24.916 --> 00:16:27.214
You're going to make a move
against Koval, aren't you?

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:30.050
You're going to find
a way to use his illness

00:16:30.088 --> 00:16:31.715
to keep him off the Committee.

00:16:31.756 --> 00:16:33.951
I suppose it would be
naive of me to point out

00:16:33.992 --> 00:16:35.892
that interfering
in the internal affairs

00:16:35.927 --> 00:16:37.053
of a sovereign power

00:16:37.095 --> 00:16:40.264
is explicitly forbidden
by the Federation Charter.

00:16:40.397 --> 00:16:44.060
Without confirming or denying
your speculation

00:16:44.101 --> 00:16:47.161
I will say
that if Koval comes to power

00:16:47.204 --> 00:16:49.365
it'd be a disaster
for the Federation.

00:16:49.406 --> 00:16:52.500
He'll argue for the Romulans
to abrogate the alliance

00:16:52.542 --> 00:16:54.703
and negotiate a separate peace
with the Dominion

00:16:54.745 --> 00:16:56.178
and I don't think
I need to tell you

00:16:56.213 --> 00:16:58.306
what that would do
to the course of the war.

00:16:58.348 --> 00:16:59.781
You can't justify that
by manipulating...

00:16:59.816 --> 00:17:01.909
Let's make a deal, Doctor...

00:17:02.019 --> 00:17:05.455
I'll spare you the ends-
justify-the-means speech

00:17:05.489 --> 00:17:06.751
and you spare me

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.815
the we-must-do-
what's-right speech.

00:17:08.859 --> 00:17:11.828
You and I are not going to see
eye to eye on this subject

00:17:11.862 --> 00:17:13.727
so I suggest
we stop discussing it.

00:17:13.764 --> 00:17:16.733
This mission is reconnaissance.

00:17:16.767 --> 00:17:18.359
We are not going
to be called upon

00:17:18.402 --> 00:17:20.131
to do anything other than that.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.638
Now, why don't you
get some rest?

00:17:22.673 --> 00:17:25.233
We'll be in orbit
of Romulus by 0600

00:17:25.275 --> 00:17:27.607
and you will need to have
your wits about you.

00:17:50.801 --> 00:17:52.598
Here you are, sir.

00:17:59.209 --> 00:18:01.074
Dr. Julian Bashir?

00:18:01.111 --> 00:18:02.738
Yes.

00:18:02.779 --> 00:18:04.110
I understand
you were the officer

00:18:04.147 --> 00:18:05.774
who first identified
the biogenic weapon

00:18:05.816 --> 00:18:06.908
known as the Quickening.

00:18:07.017 --> 00:18:08.109
That's right...

00:18:08.151 --> 00:18:10.085
on Boranis III,
in the Gamma Quadrant.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:11.917
I don't believe
we've been introduced.

00:18:11.955 --> 00:18:13.923
Koval.

00:18:13.957 --> 00:18:15.288
Well, it's a pleasure
to meet you.

00:18:15.325 --> 00:18:16.417
Why?

00:18:17.427 --> 00:18:18.826
Well, you've got me there.

00:18:18.862 --> 00:18:21.626
It's just a simple
form of expression, I suppose.

00:18:21.665 --> 00:18:23.064
And like most human expressions

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.931
completely devoid of meaning.

00:18:24.968 --> 00:18:27.937
Can the Dominion's Quickening
virus be replicated?

00:18:28.004 --> 00:18:30.700
We've had a little difficulty
in, uh, recreating

00:18:30.741 --> 00:18:32.538
the exact RNA sequence
of the virus

00:18:32.576 --> 00:18:35.067
which is why we've been
unable to develop a vaccine.

00:18:35.112 --> 00:18:37.103
However, there are alternate
methods of making vaccines...

00:18:37.147 --> 00:18:39.342
I'm not interested
in the vaccine.

00:18:39.383 --> 00:18:41.146
I'm interested in the virus.

00:18:41.184 --> 00:18:42.515
Do you know how to introduce

00:18:42.552 --> 00:18:44.179
the Quickening
into a population?

00:18:45.389 --> 00:18:46.515
Basically.

00:18:46.556 --> 00:18:47.648
Good.

00:18:47.691 --> 00:18:49.556
I look forward
to hearing your lecture.

00:18:55.932 --> 00:18:58.662
You're going to make
a very fine operative, Doctor.

00:18:58.702 --> 00:18:59.964
I beg your pardon?

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.435
The Chairman of the Tal Shiar

00:19:01.471 --> 00:19:03.234
rarely speaks
with anyone in public...

00:19:03.273 --> 00:19:05.707
much less someone
wearing that uniform.

00:19:05.742 --> 00:19:08.575
Starfleet Intelligence
should recruit you immediately.

00:19:08.612 --> 00:19:10.807
What makes you think I'm not
working for them already?

00:19:10.847 --> 00:19:14.476
Somehow, it wouldn't surprise me
if half the people in this room

00:19:14.518 --> 00:19:16.213
turned out to be operatives.

00:19:16.253 --> 00:19:17.515
You are joking.

00:19:17.554 --> 00:19:20.022
It may be impolitic to say this

00:19:20.056 --> 00:19:23.787
but there are those who believe
the alliance is merely a...

00:19:23.827 --> 00:19:25.590
momentary truce.

00:19:25.629 --> 00:19:27.062
And are you one of them?

00:19:27.097 --> 00:19:28.758
Well, I could ask you
the same thing.

00:19:28.799 --> 00:19:30.733
Well, in my case,
it's a firm "no"

00:19:30.767 --> 00:19:31.927
but you've answered
my question...

00:19:32.035 --> 00:19:33.195
with a question.

00:19:33.236 --> 00:19:35.727
I try not to predict
the future.

00:19:35.772 --> 00:19:37.797
What about Chairman Koval?

00:19:37.841 --> 00:19:38.830
You tell me.

00:19:38.875 --> 00:19:39.864
You just spoke with him.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:41.935
That's more than I've
done in six months.

00:19:41.978 --> 00:19:43.741
I take it you two
don't get along.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.509
We have different views.

00:19:45.549 --> 00:19:46.880
Which are?

00:19:49.352 --> 00:19:50.944
State secrets.

00:19:50.987 --> 00:19:52.511
Naturally.

00:19:54.458 --> 00:19:57.518
This is an adult female
inhabitant of Boranis III.

00:19:57.561 --> 00:20:00.758
The markings on the face
are typical of a humanoid

00:20:00.797 --> 00:20:02.424
who's been infected
by the disease

00:20:02.466 --> 00:20:05.833
but who has not yet entered
the terminal stage.

00:20:05.869 --> 00:20:07.860
In this next photograph

00:20:07.904 --> 00:20:10.896
you can tell by the necrotic
nature of the lesions

00:20:10.941 --> 00:20:13.273
that the patient has, indeed,
entered the terminal stage

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.436
of the disease.

00:20:14.478 --> 00:20:15.706
This is also marked

00:20:15.745 --> 00:20:18.305
by an increase
in leukocyte production.

00:20:18.348 --> 00:20:19.906
Thank you, Doctor.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.417
Excellent.

00:20:21.451 --> 00:20:22.418
Thank you.

00:20:22.452 --> 00:20:23.544
Very enlightening.

00:20:23.587 --> 00:20:25.350
You almost made it
comprehensible.

00:20:25.388 --> 00:20:27.481
Next time, I'll do the lecture
with hand puppets just for you.

00:20:27.524 --> 00:20:28.650
Thank you very much.

00:20:28.692 --> 00:20:30.819
I'm glad to see you still
have your sense of humor.

00:20:30.861 --> 00:20:33.989
I trust you noticed who was
sitting in the front row.

00:20:34.097 --> 00:20:37.362
Yes. He came to see me this
morning between sessions.

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:39.994
He wanted to know more
about the Quickening...

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:42.231
specifically, if I knew
how to replicate the virus

00:20:42.272 --> 00:20:44.240
and how to introduce it
into a population.

00:20:44.274 --> 00:20:46.174
What did you think
of his health?

00:20:46.209 --> 00:20:47.574
Didn't you hear
what I just said?

00:20:48.945 --> 00:20:50.207
I heard you.

00:20:50.247 --> 00:20:52.545
Koval wants to get his
hands on the Quickening.

00:20:52.582 --> 00:20:54.311
That's not news to me...

00:20:54.351 --> 00:20:55.784
that the head of the Tal Shiar

00:20:55.819 --> 00:20:57.650
is interested
in biogenic weapons.

00:20:57.687 --> 00:21:00.747
Pull your head out of the sand
and take a look around, Doctor.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:03.156
These are not nice people
we're dealing with here.

00:21:03.193 --> 00:21:05.058
Now answer my question.

00:21:05.095 --> 00:21:07.825
His eyelids were
slightly displaced.

00:21:07.864 --> 00:21:09.957
He had a noticeable weakness
in the facial muscles...

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:10.967
probably the result

00:21:11.001 --> 00:21:13.128
of a compromised
neuromuscular function...

00:21:13.169 --> 00:21:15.603
and his respiration
was somewhat irregular.

00:21:15.639 --> 00:21:17.300
Bottom line.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.967
He may have Tuvan Syndrome.

00:21:19.075 --> 00:21:22.067
But if he does,
it's in the very early stages.

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:25.771
How long does he have?

00:21:25.815 --> 00:21:28.841
If his case fits the profile

00:21:28.885 --> 00:21:32.343
he will start experiencing
a loss of motor skills

00:21:32.389 --> 00:21:34.118
in ten to 15 years...

00:21:34.157 --> 00:21:37.593
with a life expectancy
in the 20 to 25-year range.

00:21:37.627 --> 00:21:40.255
Are there instances
in which the disease

00:21:40.297 --> 00:21:42.197
accelerates without warning?

00:21:42.232 --> 00:21:45.429
It happens, but in less than
five percent of the cases.

00:21:45.468 --> 00:21:48.801
Is there anything that could
trigger the acceleration?

00:21:48.838 --> 00:21:52.968
You know... I don't know
what you're asking me.

00:21:53.009 --> 00:21:55.000
Never mind.

00:21:55.045 --> 00:21:56.444
Thank you, Doctor.

00:21:56.479 --> 00:21:58.344
You've been very helpful.

00:22:03.219 --> 00:22:04.516
This is unbelievable.

00:22:04.554 --> 00:22:05.885
Let's put aside for the moment

00:22:05.922 --> 00:22:07.355
that he's contemplating
the murder

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:08.687
of a high-ranking official.

00:22:08.725 --> 00:22:10.522
What in the hell makes him think

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:11.959
that the next head
of the Tal Shiar

00:22:12.062 --> 00:22:13.689
would be any better than Koval?

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:15.357
Well, Sloan's more
concerned with who gets

00:22:15.398 --> 00:22:17.389
the empty seat on the
Continuing Committee.

00:22:17.434 --> 00:22:18.958
He's hoping
that Cretak gets that.

00:22:19.035 --> 00:22:20.900
Well, I sort of agree
with him there.

00:22:20.937 --> 00:22:22.632
Cretak, for all her abrasiveness

00:22:22.672 --> 00:22:23.969
is at least a patriot.

00:22:24.007 --> 00:22:25.736
What makes her any different
from Koval?

00:22:25.775 --> 00:22:27.970
If you saw the reports
from Starfleet Intelligence

00:22:28.078 --> 00:22:30.137
that I see, you would
never ask that question.

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:31.943
Koval would like nothing better

00:22:31.982 --> 00:22:34.678
than to see the Romulan
banner waving over Earth.

00:22:34.718 --> 00:22:38.484
Believe me, Doctor,
Chairman Koval is not someone

00:22:38.521 --> 00:22:40.716
we want to see
at the Praetor's right hand.

00:22:40.757 --> 00:22:43.726
I'll have Sloan confined
to his quarters immediately

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.352
but that may not
solve our problem.

00:22:45.395 --> 00:22:46.521
Sir?

00:22:48.498 --> 00:22:49.795
Has it occurred to you

00:22:49.833 --> 00:22:51.994
that you and Sloan may not
be the only ones here

00:22:52.035 --> 00:22:54.265
working for Section 31?

00:22:54.304 --> 00:22:56.431
For all we know,
he has a confederate

00:22:56.473 --> 00:22:58.168
somewhere in the delegation.

00:22:58.208 --> 00:22:59.641
Sloan did say that our mission

00:22:59.676 --> 00:23:01.371
would be strictly
reconnaissance...

00:23:01.411 --> 00:23:03.345
that we wouldn't be called
upon to do anything else.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.938
That could suggest
another operative...

00:23:05.048 --> 00:23:07.573
someone whose mission isn't
limited to reconnaissance.

00:23:07.617 --> 00:23:09.380
If that's true,
it could be anyone...

00:23:09.419 --> 00:23:11.683
even a member of
the Bellerophon crew.

00:23:11.721 --> 00:23:13.621
Or a Romulan.

00:23:13.657 --> 00:23:14.624
What?

00:23:14.658 --> 00:23:17.855
Sir, I believe Sloan
has an accomplice

00:23:17.894 --> 00:23:20.124
here... on Romulus.

00:23:20.163 --> 00:23:21.460
What makes you say that?

00:23:21.498 --> 00:23:22.465
Two things.

00:23:22.499 --> 00:23:25.730
First, Sloan has
too much information

00:23:25.769 --> 00:23:27.896
on the inner workings
of their government...

00:23:27.937 --> 00:23:30.599
too many insights into
their political process.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.871
Second,
Sloan's plan is to kill Koval

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:34.877
while making it appear to be

00:23:34.911 --> 00:23:36.674
an accelerated case
of Tuvan Syndrome.

00:23:36.713 --> 00:23:38.738
Now, the only way to do that
would be to expose Koval

00:23:38.782 --> 00:23:41.376
to a short burst
of nadion radiation.

00:23:41.418 --> 00:23:44.649
The simplest plan would be to
maneuver him near a phaser relay

00:23:44.688 --> 00:23:46.986
and surreptitiously
irradiate him.

00:23:47.057 --> 00:23:49.150
Now, since I doubt very much

00:23:49.192 --> 00:23:51.217
that Sloan is going to have
the chance to do that

00:23:51.261 --> 00:23:54.253
it stands to reason someone else
is going to have to.

00:23:54.297 --> 00:23:55.491
A Romulan?

00:23:55.532 --> 00:23:56.658
Exactly.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:00.363
Sir, Sloan may have already
gotten things underway.

00:24:00.403 --> 00:24:01.597
We have to warn them.

00:24:01.638 --> 00:24:05.665
And how am I supposed to explain
Section 31 to the Romulans?

00:24:05.709 --> 00:24:07.540
All hell would break loose
if they hear

00:24:07.577 --> 00:24:09.772
that there's a rogue
Federation agency running around

00:24:09.813 --> 00:24:11.280
plotting assassinations.

00:24:11.314 --> 00:24:13.578
It could bring
the alliance down.

00:24:13.616 --> 00:24:16.084
Besides, all we have
is speculation

00:24:16.119 --> 00:24:17.609
- at this point.
- Admiral...

00:24:17.654 --> 00:24:18.951
The answer is no.

00:24:18.988 --> 00:24:22.355
After I have Sloan arrested,
I'll break radio silence

00:24:22.392 --> 00:24:24.622
and inform Starfleet Command
of the situation.

00:24:24.661 --> 00:24:25.958
Your orders are to sit tight

00:24:26.062 --> 00:24:27.927
and do nothing
until you hear from me.

00:24:27.964 --> 00:24:29.454
Aye, sir.

00:24:48.551 --> 00:24:49.540
I don't know.

00:24:49.586 --> 00:24:51.713
Jepella said she went
in to deliver a report

00:24:51.755 --> 00:24:53.746
and found him slumped
over his desk.

00:24:53.790 --> 00:24:55.451
Do they have any idea
what happened?

00:24:55.492 --> 00:24:57.221
Dr. Frame said it looked
like an aneurysm

00:24:57.260 --> 00:24:58.420
but they're still running tests.

00:24:58.461 --> 00:24:59.428
An aneurysm.

00:24:59.462 --> 00:25:00.486
I saw the Admiral this morning.

00:25:00.530 --> 00:25:01.497
He looked fine.

00:25:01.531 --> 00:25:02.691
They say that's
the way it happens.

00:25:02.732 --> 00:25:04.097
Which Admiral are
you talking about?

00:25:04.134 --> 00:25:06.125
Uh, Admiral Ross, sir.

00:25:06.169 --> 00:25:07.431
He collapsed at his desk.

00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:08.459
Where is he?

00:25:08.505 --> 00:25:09.699
Sick Bay.

00:25:15.411 --> 00:25:17.174
Hey.

00:25:42.605 --> 00:25:44.664
I can't trust anybody
aboard the Bellerophon.

00:25:44.707 --> 00:25:46.675
And I can't contact DS9.

00:25:46.709 --> 00:25:49.644
For security reasons, there's
been a communications blackout.

00:25:49.679 --> 00:25:52.204
Senator, I have no one
else to turn to.

00:25:52.248 --> 00:25:53.442
I need your help.

00:25:53.483 --> 00:25:54.745
To do what?

00:25:54.784 --> 00:25:56.342
I have reason to believe

00:25:56.386 --> 00:25:59.583
that Sloan has an accomplice
within the Romulan government.

00:25:59.622 --> 00:26:02.056
Someone who's going to help him
carry out this assassination.

00:26:04.694 --> 00:26:07.663
Koval has been saying
there's a traitor in the Senate.

00:26:07.697 --> 00:26:10.097
Someone working for
Starfleet Intelligence.

00:26:10.133 --> 00:26:12.158
Section 31 isn't part
of Starfleet Intelligence.

00:26:12.202 --> 00:26:14.193
They are Federation
citizens working

00:26:14.237 --> 00:26:15.727
to advance your interests.

00:26:15.772 --> 00:26:17.933
That makes them
your responsibility.

00:26:18.041 --> 00:26:19.633
You're absolutely right.

00:26:19.676 --> 00:26:21.837
That's why I'm doing everything
I can to stop them.

00:26:21.878 --> 00:26:23.277
I'm trying to convince Sloan

00:26:23.313 --> 00:26:25.406
that Koval doesn't
have Tuvan Syndrome

00:26:25.448 --> 00:26:27.939
but he may have already asked
his accomplice to proceed.

00:26:28.051 --> 00:26:30.212
So if we want to be sure
to stop this assassination

00:26:30.253 --> 00:26:32.687
we have to find Sloan's
Romulan accomplice.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:34.651
And you expect me
to find this traitor.

00:26:34.689 --> 00:26:37.715
Sloan said something about Koval
having a personal database.

00:26:37.758 --> 00:26:38.782
It stands to reason

00:26:38.826 --> 00:26:41.420
that it contains a list
of potential suspects.

00:26:41.462 --> 00:26:42.793
Now, is there any possible way

00:26:42.830 --> 00:26:44.525
you can get me
a copy of this database

00:26:44.565 --> 00:26:46.430
so that I can run
an analysis of...

00:26:46.467 --> 00:26:49.129
You are asking me to hand
over secret documents.

00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:50.603
I'm asking you to put aside

00:26:50.638 --> 00:26:52.799
three centuries of mistrust
between our peoples

00:26:52.840 --> 00:26:54.501
and help me stop a murder.

00:26:54.542 --> 00:26:57.534
Senator, if we can't reach out

00:26:57.578 --> 00:26:59.205
and bridge the gulf
that is between us

00:26:59.246 --> 00:27:02.647
if we can't trust each other,
a man will die

00:27:02.683 --> 00:27:05.117
and we will be
partially responsible.

00:27:06.120 --> 00:27:07.917
I need your help.

00:27:08.022 --> 00:27:09.751
Please.

00:27:17.998 --> 00:27:19.431
You wanted to see me, Doctor?

00:27:19.467 --> 00:27:20.764
Yes.

00:27:20.801 --> 00:27:23.929
I'm not convinced that Koval is
suffering from Tuvan Syndrome.

00:27:24.038 --> 00:27:25.300
His symptoms could be the result

00:27:25.339 --> 00:27:27.204
of any number of different
health problems.

00:27:28.275 --> 00:27:30.140
You didn't say that before.

00:27:30.177 --> 00:27:32.611
Well, I'm not an expert
on Romulan physiology.

00:27:32.646 --> 00:27:34.637
Most of my knowledge
on Tuvan Syndrome

00:27:34.682 --> 00:27:36.877
comes from studies
done on Vulcan patients.

00:27:36.917 --> 00:27:37.884
I thought Vulcans

00:27:37.918 --> 00:27:41.183
and Romulans
were virtually identical.

00:27:41.222 --> 00:27:42.712
Yes, but there are

00:27:42.757 --> 00:27:44.816
some important
genetic differences.

00:27:44.859 --> 00:27:46.326
And the more I study

00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:48.351
the available data
on Romulan physiology

00:27:48.395 --> 00:27:50.829
the less sure I am that
my diagnosis was correct.

00:27:50.865 --> 00:27:52.560
How could you find out
for sure?

00:27:52.600 --> 00:27:54.500
The best way would be
to do an examination

00:27:54.535 --> 00:27:56.400
but I hardly think
he'll agree to that.

00:27:56.437 --> 00:27:59.634
What if you obtained
a sample of his skin cells?

00:27:59.673 --> 00:28:01.641
Could you run an analysis?

00:28:01.675 --> 00:28:03.336
Probably.

00:28:03.377 --> 00:28:05.038
But how do you propose...

00:28:05.079 --> 00:28:08.913
We'll treat your palm
with a microcellular adhesive.

00:28:08.949 --> 00:28:10.712
The next time
you shake his hand

00:28:10.751 --> 00:28:12.548
you'll get your sample.

00:28:15.022 --> 00:28:16.284
All right.

00:28:35.810 --> 00:28:37.300
Mr. Chairman.

00:28:37.344 --> 00:28:39.505
What a pleasure
to see you again.

00:28:42.416 --> 00:28:44.884
I'd be very happy to resume
our discussion on the Quickening

00:28:44.919 --> 00:28:46.409
before this conference
is adjourned.

00:28:46.453 --> 00:28:48.785
I believe you answered
all my questions, Doctor.

00:28:48.823 --> 00:28:51.724
Well, I'm glad
to have been able to help.

00:28:51.759 --> 00:28:53.886
Doctor, I would like to have

00:28:53.928 --> 00:28:56.590
a word with you
on another matter.

00:28:56.630 --> 00:28:57.597
In private.

00:28:57.631 --> 00:28:58.757
Of course.

00:28:58.799 --> 00:29:00.528
I believe
the Lecture Hall's empty.

00:29:00.568 --> 00:29:01.899
We have other, more comfortable

00:29:01.969 --> 00:29:03.664
facilities available,
if you please.

00:29:10.978 --> 00:29:12.070
Sit down.

00:29:17.351 --> 00:29:19.911
I can assure you that you
will be sitting in that chair

00:29:19.987 --> 00:29:21.784
one way or the other, Doctor.

00:29:34.835 --> 00:29:38.430
Now we'll have our private talk.

00:29:38.472 --> 00:29:40.303
What shall we talk about?

00:29:40.341 --> 00:29:42.241
Why you're really on Romulus.

00:29:42.276 --> 00:29:43.937
Who you're working for,
and, of course

00:29:44.044 --> 00:29:45.375
who's helping you.

00:29:45.412 --> 00:29:46.572
Don't worry...

00:29:46.614 --> 00:29:49.139
I won't waste your time
with pointless questions.

00:30:00.527 --> 00:30:02.085
This can be painful or not.

00:30:02.129 --> 00:30:03.596
That's up to you, Doctor.

00:30:03.631 --> 00:30:06.964
Either way, I will know
what you know.

00:30:25.252 --> 00:30:27.618
It appears that your brain's
neurocellular structure

00:30:27.655 --> 00:30:29.987
is not susceptible
to our scanning techniques.

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:32.081
Evidently a result
of the genetic enhancements

00:30:32.126 --> 00:30:33.991
made to your parietal cortex.

00:30:34.061 --> 00:30:35.221
Sorry.

00:30:35.262 --> 00:30:37.492
I do have other methods
at my disposal

00:30:37.531 --> 00:30:40.398
but it would save everyone
a great deal of trouble

00:30:40.434 --> 00:30:42.595
if you would simply tell
me what I want to know.

00:30:42.636 --> 00:30:45.002
You haven't asked me
any questions yet.

00:30:45.039 --> 00:30:47.269
I think you know what
I'm interested in.

00:30:47.308 --> 00:30:49.003
Who are you working for?

00:30:49.076 --> 00:30:50.941
Why are you here?

00:30:53.547 --> 00:30:54.536
Bring him.

00:31:03.090 --> 00:31:05.320
Dr. Julian Bashir.

00:31:05.359 --> 00:31:07.657
You are appearing before
the Continuing Committee

00:31:07.695 --> 00:31:09.925
of the Romulan people.

00:31:09.964 --> 00:31:12.694
Any statements will be made
part of the official record.

00:31:12.733 --> 00:31:15.293
Senator Cretak
is charged with attempting

00:31:15.336 --> 00:31:19.534
to access a Tal Shiar database
without proper authorization.

00:31:19.573 --> 00:31:24.601
The Senator has told the
Committee a remarkable story.

00:31:24.645 --> 00:31:27.637
Since you are a key figure
in her story

00:31:27.681 --> 00:31:30.844
we are most eager to hear
your version of events.

00:31:37.458 --> 00:31:40.359
What I am about to say
may be shocking.

00:31:40.394 --> 00:31:42.624
It may even damage the relations

00:31:42.663 --> 00:31:44.995
between our two peoples

00:31:45.032 --> 00:31:46.465
but it's the truth.

00:31:48.702 --> 00:31:51.569
A few days ago,
I became aware of a plot

00:31:51.605 --> 00:31:53.596
to assassinate Chairman Koval.

00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:56.438
It was conceived of
by a man known to me

00:31:56.477 --> 00:31:58.138
only as "Sloan."

00:31:58.178 --> 00:32:02.342
He works for an organization
called Section 31.

00:32:02.383 --> 00:32:06.114
They see themselves
as protecting the interests

00:32:06.153 --> 00:32:07.347
of the Federation

00:32:07.388 --> 00:32:11.882
although they have absolutely
no official standing.

00:32:13.327 --> 00:32:16.888
Once I realized what Sloan
was attempting to do

00:32:16.930 --> 00:32:19.956
I contacted Senator Cretak

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:23.197
in order to enlist her aid
in stopping him.

00:32:23.237 --> 00:32:24.761
Why her?

00:32:24.805 --> 00:32:27.137
I had no one else to turn to.

00:32:27.174 --> 00:32:29.904
I was unable to contact
Deep Space 9

00:32:29.943 --> 00:32:33.106
and I couldn't trust anybody
aboard the Bellerophon.

00:32:33.147 --> 00:32:36.173
But you felt that you could
trust a Romulan Senator?

00:32:36.216 --> 00:32:37.649
Yes.

00:32:37.684 --> 00:32:39.982
For all our differences

00:32:40.020 --> 00:32:41.112
I do respect her.

00:32:44.058 --> 00:32:45.320
Continue.

00:32:45.359 --> 00:32:47.953
For reasons that are
extremely complicated

00:32:47.995 --> 00:32:49.223
I came to believe

00:32:49.263 --> 00:32:50.855
that there's a traitor
in your government

00:32:50.898 --> 00:32:51.865
working for Section 31.

00:32:51.899 --> 00:32:54.697
I asked the Senator
to obtain the database

00:32:54.735 --> 00:32:56.999
so that we could
expose this person

00:32:57.071 --> 00:32:59.005
and prevent the assassination.

00:32:59.106 --> 00:33:02.303
Senator Cretak,
why didn't you come to me

00:33:02.342 --> 00:33:04.037
with this information?

00:33:04.078 --> 00:33:08.037
I was afraid that if word
of this... plot... got out

00:33:08.082 --> 00:33:10.209
it would destroy the alliance.

00:33:10.250 --> 00:33:12.411
I decided to keep
my own counsel.

00:33:14.555 --> 00:33:16.546
I regret that decision.

00:33:16.590 --> 00:33:18.956
As well you should, Kimara.

00:33:19.059 --> 00:33:21.789
It's an interesting story

00:33:21.829 --> 00:33:23.729
but it's not the whole story.

00:33:23.764 --> 00:33:26.324
If I may be permitted
to bring in another witness?

00:33:29.169 --> 00:33:30.830
Bring in prisoner 527.

00:33:36.910 --> 00:33:38.070
Praetor

00:33:38.112 --> 00:33:40.603
this is the man
known as "Sloan."

00:33:40.647 --> 00:33:42.547
Unlike the Doctor, his mind is

00:33:42.583 --> 00:33:45.143
quite susceptible
to our data-retrieval methods.

00:33:45.185 --> 00:33:46.550
Under questioning,
he has confirmed

00:33:46.587 --> 00:33:48.851
much of what the Doctor
and the Senator have told you

00:33:48.889 --> 00:33:50.948
with one
important exception...

00:33:50.991 --> 00:33:53.152
there is no Section 31.

00:33:53.193 --> 00:33:55.991
Sloan, in fact, works
for Starfleet Intelligence.

00:33:56.029 --> 00:33:59.521
Far from being the master
of a rogue agency

00:33:59.566 --> 00:34:01.397
he is simply one
of many operatives

00:34:01.435 --> 00:34:03.096
in the employ
of the Federation.

00:34:03.137 --> 00:34:05.196
He's had a long career.

00:34:05.239 --> 00:34:07.366
Most of which
is still unknown to us.

00:34:07.407 --> 00:34:09.773
However, there is one
interesting element

00:34:09.810 --> 00:34:12.108
that we do know...
he was the protégé

00:34:12.146 --> 00:34:14.341
of the late
Vice Admiral Fujisaki.

00:34:14.381 --> 00:34:17.509
Sloan did not take
the death of his mentor well.

00:34:17.551 --> 00:34:18.540
He came to believe

00:34:18.585 --> 00:34:20.450
he was murdered
by the Tal Shiar.

00:34:20.487 --> 00:34:22.682
In his eyes, the assassination

00:34:22.723 --> 00:34:26.386
of a Starfleet Admiral was
"stepping over the line."

00:34:26.426 --> 00:34:28.417
Isn't that the phrase?

00:34:28.462 --> 00:34:32.865
After Fujisaki's death, he
was confronted with a dilemma.

00:34:32.900 --> 00:34:34.959
How could he seek vengeance

00:34:35.002 --> 00:34:37.232
without violating
the Federation's laws?

00:34:37.271 --> 00:34:39.865
His answer was
to invent Section 31...

00:34:39.907 --> 00:34:42.967
a rogue organization
that answered to no one.

00:34:43.010 --> 00:34:44.477
If they killed the head

00:34:44.511 --> 00:34:46.308
of the Tal Shiar,
Starfleet Intelligence

00:34:46.346 --> 00:34:47.870
would be held blameless.

00:34:47.915 --> 00:34:50.475
As the Committee knows

00:34:50.517 --> 00:34:52.985
I have been diagnosed
with Tuvan Syndrome.

00:34:53.086 --> 00:34:54.815
Sloan became aware
of my condition

00:34:54.855 --> 00:34:56.220
and hoped to make my death

00:34:56.256 --> 00:34:58.281
Iook like a sudden
acceleration of the disease.

00:34:58.325 --> 00:35:01.158
To do that,
he needed a doctor.

00:35:01.195 --> 00:35:05.495
Sloan arranged to recruit
Dr. Bashir into Section 31.

00:35:05.532 --> 00:35:08.763
After that, Sloan
bided his time

00:35:08.802 --> 00:35:11.270
and waited for an opportunity
to present itself.

00:35:11.305 --> 00:35:13.796
He found one when he learned
of this conference.

00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:17.207
He then arranged
for Bashir to be invited.

00:35:17.244 --> 00:35:18.939
Everything was going perfectly

00:35:19.012 --> 00:35:22.470
but then he made
a fatal mistake.

00:35:22.516 --> 00:35:25.610
He decided to come
to Romulus himself.

00:35:25.652 --> 00:35:28.746
He was unaware that his identity
had become known to us.

00:35:28.789 --> 00:35:30.723
Once we recognized him
in the delegation

00:35:30.757 --> 00:35:32.054
we knew immediately

00:35:32.092 --> 00:35:33.753
that an intelligence
operation was underway.

00:35:33.794 --> 00:35:37.730
What I don't understand
is... why.

00:35:37.764 --> 00:35:40.699
Why did you come here and take
the risk of being discovered?

00:35:42.469 --> 00:35:45.700
I had to make sure
nothing went wrong

00:35:45.739 --> 00:35:49.698
and I wanted to watch you die...

00:35:50.944 --> 00:35:53.344
You broke the cardinal
rule of our profession.

00:35:53.380 --> 00:35:55.905
You allowed business
to become personal.

00:35:57.651 --> 00:35:59.983
So there was
an assassination plan?

00:36:00.020 --> 00:36:01.920
Most definitely.

00:36:02.022 --> 00:36:04.752
As to the involvement
of the Doctor and the Senator

00:36:04.791 --> 00:36:07.259
Dr. Bashir may have
intended to kill me

00:36:07.294 --> 00:36:08.727
or he may have
intended to save me.

00:36:08.762 --> 00:36:10.696
There is no way
to know for certain.

00:36:10.731 --> 00:36:12.528
As for Senator Cretak

00:36:12.566 --> 00:36:15.126
we all know
she's an ambitious woman.

00:36:15.168 --> 00:36:16.430
It is entirely possible,
she would

00:36:16.470 --> 00:36:18.165
welcome my death,
especially if it meant

00:36:18.205 --> 00:36:20.173
her being elevated
to the Continuing Committee

00:36:20.207 --> 00:36:21.538
in my place.

00:36:21.575 --> 00:36:23.475
That is a lie, Koval.

00:36:23.510 --> 00:36:25.307
I was trying to save your life.

00:36:25.345 --> 00:36:27.438
Well, then,
you're simply a fool.

00:36:27.481 --> 00:36:30.211
You let a Starfleet Intelligence
officer manipulate you

00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:32.343
into committing
an act of treason.

00:36:39.925 --> 00:36:41.085
It is the finding

00:36:41.127 --> 00:36:45.860
of this Committee that
Senator Cretak has conspired

00:36:45.898 --> 00:36:47.559
to commit treason
against the state.

00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:50.068
Sentence to be determined
at a later date.

00:36:51.203 --> 00:36:53.831
Dr. Bashir will be returned
to the Bellerophon.

00:36:53.873 --> 00:36:54.931
Mr. Sloan...

00:36:54.974 --> 00:36:58.705
is remanded to the custody
of the Tal Shiar

00:36:58.744 --> 00:37:00.405
for further interrogation.

00:37:00.446 --> 00:37:01.435
No!

00:37:30.476 --> 00:37:31.807
Come in.

00:37:33.813 --> 00:37:35.075
Admiral.

00:37:35.114 --> 00:37:36.581
Doctor.

00:37:37.850 --> 00:37:40.250
Feeling, uh, better, sir?

00:37:40.286 --> 00:37:41.275
Much.

00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:43.948
Dr. Frame tells me
that I should take it easy

00:37:44.023 --> 00:37:45.354
for a few days,
but, uh... paperwork

00:37:45.391 --> 00:37:46.881
waits for no man.

00:37:46.926 --> 00:37:48.223
What can I do for you?

00:37:48.260 --> 00:37:49.625
I have a question.

00:37:49.662 --> 00:37:51.220
Where's Sloan?

00:37:52.264 --> 00:37:53.754
Sloan's dead.

00:37:53.799 --> 00:37:57.963
Admiral... where's Sloan?

00:38:02.074 --> 00:38:04.133
If we're going to have
this discussion

00:38:04.176 --> 00:38:05.973
then it's off the record.

00:38:11.684 --> 00:38:14.847
But before I answer your
question, answer mine.

00:38:16.322 --> 00:38:17.880
How did you know?

00:38:17.923 --> 00:38:20.653
The man Koval described
was not the same man

00:38:20.693 --> 00:38:23.526
who recruited me
into Section 31.

00:38:23.562 --> 00:38:26.463
Anyone clever enough
to pull the wool

00:38:26.498 --> 00:38:28.398
so completely over my eyes

00:38:28.434 --> 00:38:31.028
wouldn't have been caught
by the Romulans so easily.

00:38:31.070 --> 00:38:33.766
There had to be
another explanation.

00:38:33.806 --> 00:38:36.570
And then I remembered
that you were the one

00:38:36.609 --> 00:38:38.839
who planted the idea
in my head

00:38:38.878 --> 00:38:41.403
that Sloan had an accomplice.

00:38:41.447 --> 00:38:44.143
You were the one who didn't
want to tell the Romulans

00:38:44.183 --> 00:38:46.048
that there was
an assassination plot.

00:38:46.085 --> 00:38:48.952
You were the one
who issued the orders

00:38:49.054 --> 00:38:50.954
preventing me from contacting
Deep Space 9.

00:38:52.391 --> 00:38:55.883
And when the time
came to arrest Sloan

00:38:55.928 --> 00:39:02.697
you conveniently had an
aneurysm... leaving me alone

00:39:02.735 --> 00:39:06.728
with no one to turn to
for help, except Cretak

00:39:06.772 --> 00:39:09.400
and as I realized
your involvement

00:39:09.441 --> 00:39:12.604
the rest began
to fall into place.

00:39:12.645 --> 00:39:14.306
Where is he?

00:39:16.415 --> 00:39:17.677
I don't know.

00:39:17.716 --> 00:39:20.844
But he's alive...
isn't he?

00:39:20.886 --> 00:39:23.446
He was supposed
to be beamed away

00:39:23.489 --> 00:39:25.719
a split second
before the phaser beam hit him.

00:39:25.758 --> 00:39:29.785
Whether it worked or not,
I couldn't say.

00:39:29.828 --> 00:39:34.322
How long has Koval
been working for Starfleet?

00:39:34.366 --> 00:39:36.129
He's been providing
the Federation

00:39:36.168 --> 00:39:40.036
with critical military
intelligence for over a year.

00:39:40.072 --> 00:39:44.532
When he started working
with Section 31, I don't know.

00:39:44.576 --> 00:39:48.512
But in any case,
we have our mole...

00:39:48.547 --> 00:39:50.139
working for us

00:39:50.182 --> 00:39:52.946
at the top levels
of Romulan government.

00:39:53.052 --> 00:39:55.612
Good for us.

00:39:57.289 --> 00:40:01.521
And what about your friend,
Senator Cretak?

00:40:01.560 --> 00:40:04.358
What's going to happen to her?

00:40:04.396 --> 00:40:06.830
Dismissed from the Senate...

00:40:06.865 --> 00:40:08.560
definitely.

00:40:08.600 --> 00:40:10.329
Imprisoned, most likely.

00:40:10.369 --> 00:40:12.337
Executed?

00:40:13.839 --> 00:40:15.204
I hope not.

00:40:15.240 --> 00:40:17.265
You set her up!

00:40:17.309 --> 00:40:20.540
She was an innocent woman
and you let Sloan destroy her.

00:40:20.579 --> 00:40:21.568
Why?

00:40:21.613 --> 00:40:24.480
She believed in the alliance.

00:40:26.218 --> 00:40:27.845
She was on our side.

00:40:29.121 --> 00:40:31.089
No, she wasn't.

00:40:31.123 --> 00:40:32.750
I told you before, Julian...

00:40:32.791 --> 00:40:33.985
she's a patriot

00:40:34.026 --> 00:40:36.256
which means, if it serves
the interests of the Romulans

00:40:36.295 --> 00:40:38.729
to negotiate a separate
peace with the Dominion

00:40:38.764 --> 00:40:40.857
Cretak would push that option

00:40:40.899 --> 00:40:43.993
and believe me, the Dominion
would like nothing more

00:40:44.036 --> 00:40:46.436
than to make a deal with
the Romulans right now.

00:40:46.472 --> 00:40:49.669
So Koval becomes your guarantee
that that does not happen

00:40:49.708 --> 00:40:51.005
and as a man
who was nearly killed

00:40:51.076 --> 00:40:52.441
for his anti-Federation
activities

00:40:52.478 --> 00:40:54.002
his recommendation
to stay in the war

00:40:54.079 --> 00:40:55.273
becomes all
the more convincing.

00:40:55.314 --> 00:40:56.941
That's the general idea.

00:40:56.982 --> 00:41:00.247
And how long have you worked
for Section 31?

00:41:00.285 --> 00:41:01.252
I don't.

00:41:01.286 --> 00:41:03.686
Oh, just a temporary
alliance, is it?

00:41:03.722 --> 00:41:05.246
Something like that.

00:41:05.290 --> 00:41:08.418
You don't see anything wrong
with what happened, do you?

00:41:09.428 --> 00:41:10.759
I don't like it

00:41:10.796 --> 00:41:12.957
but I've spent the last
year and a half of my life

00:41:13.032 --> 00:41:14.897
ordering young men and
young women to die.

00:41:14.933 --> 00:41:16.457
I like that even less.

00:41:16.502 --> 00:41:18.367
That's a glib answer

00:41:18.404 --> 00:41:21.168
and a cheap way
to avoid the fact

00:41:21.206 --> 00:41:22.605
that you've trampled
on the very thing

00:41:22.641 --> 00:41:23.938
that those young men and women

00:41:23.976 --> 00:41:25.409
are out there dying to protect!

00:41:25.444 --> 00:41:27.742
Does that not mean
anything to you?!

00:41:27.780 --> 00:41:30.749
Inter arma enim silent leges.

00:41:30.783 --> 00:41:33.843
"In time of war,
the law falls silent."

00:41:33.886 --> 00:41:35.478
Cicero.

00:41:35.521 --> 00:41:38.183
So is that what we have become...

00:41:38.223 --> 00:41:40.088
a 24th-century Rome

00:41:40.125 --> 00:41:42.389
driven by nothing other
than the certainty

00:41:42.428 --> 00:41:44.862
that Caesar can do no wrong?!

00:41:47.032 --> 00:41:49.330
This conversation
never happened.

00:41:53.672 --> 00:41:54.934
You're dismissed.

00:42:20.532 --> 00:42:21.931
Good evening.

00:42:23.135 --> 00:42:25.330
Are you expecting applause?

00:42:25.370 --> 00:42:28.066
Have you come to take a bow?

00:42:28.107 --> 00:42:31.201
I just wanted to say thank you.

00:42:31.243 --> 00:42:32.642
For what?

00:42:32.678 --> 00:42:36.876
Allowing you to manipulate
me so completely?

00:42:37.950 --> 00:42:40.214
For being a decent human being.

00:42:40.252 --> 00:42:43.779
That's why we selected you
in the first place, Doctor.

00:42:43.822 --> 00:42:47.223
We needed somebody
who wanted to play the game

00:42:47.259 --> 00:42:49.159
but who'd only go so far.

00:42:49.194 --> 00:42:52.254
When the time came,
you stood your ground.

00:42:52.297 --> 00:42:53.855
You did the right thing.

00:42:53.899 --> 00:42:55.457
You reached out to an enemy.

00:42:55.501 --> 00:42:56.832
You told her the truth.

00:42:56.869 --> 00:42:58.894
You tried to stop a murder.

00:42:58.937 --> 00:43:01.599
The Federation needs
men like you, Doctor.

00:43:01.640 --> 00:43:03.938
Men of conscience.
Men of principle.

00:43:04.009 --> 00:43:06.273
Men who can sleep at night.

00:43:06.311 --> 00:43:10.543
You're also the reason
Section 31 exists.

00:43:10.582 --> 00:43:13.210
Someone has to protect
men like you

00:43:13.252 --> 00:43:16.483
from a universe
that doesn't share your sense

00:43:16.522 --> 00:43:18.319
of right and wrong.

00:43:18.357 --> 00:43:20.484
Should I feel sorry for you?

00:43:20.526 --> 00:43:22.756
Should I be weeping

00:43:22.794 --> 00:43:24.489
over the burden
you're forced to carry

00:43:24.530 --> 00:43:26.623
in order to protect
the rest of us?

00:43:30.702 --> 00:43:34.103
It is an honor
to know you, Doctor.

00:43:35.741 --> 00:43:37.038
Good night.

00:43:46.251 --> 00:43:48.446
Bashir to Security.

00:43:48.487 --> 00:43:49.852
Odo here.

00:43:53.592 --> 00:43:55.025
Never mind.

00:43:56.595 --> 00:43:57.994
My mistake.
